# "{T}: Target creature with a +1/+1 counter on it gains flying until end of turn" (CR 115.1, 122.1, 611.2a). Each player
# gives its own Woodland Changeling a +1/+1 counter with Snakeskin Veil, so the counter alone is what the target filter
# reads: Bot2's Ornithopter has none and is refused, while Bot2's Changeling is a legal target for Bot1's Tomik. Tomik taps
# as the cost, so a second activation is refused that turn; on turn 5 Tomik untaps, the opponent's Changeling has lost its
# flying at end of turn, and Bot1's own countered Changeling is a legal target. Tomik is cast on turn 1 so it is not
# summoning sick on turn 3.

